# Event data lives locally and NEVER in git.
# Four people across a 24-hour race is many GB of video, and git history
# retains every byte forever even after a delete.
/data/
*.gpx
*.tcx
manifest.json
*.manifest.json
notes*.csv
people.csv

# What the Save button downloads: one zip of notes.csv + people.csv +
# manifest.json. See filenameForSave() in src/viewer/App.tsx.
meanwhile.zip
meanwhile-*.zip

# Media, in case anything lands outside data/. This list is every extension
# ingest accepts — PHOTO_EXTENSIONS and VIDEO_EXTENSIONS in
# src/core/metadata.ts. If that set grows, grow this one with it.
#
# gitignore matching is case-sensitive, so each is listed twice: phones write
# lowercase, cameras write upper. A mixed-case name (.Jpg) would slip through
# these, which is one more reason event media belongs in /data/ rather than
# relying on this net.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.jpe
*.heic
*.heif
*.png
*.webp
*.avif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.gif
*.dng
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm
*.3gp
*.mts
*.JPG
*.JPEG
*.JPE
*.HEIC
*.HEIF
*.PNG
*.WEBP
*.AVIF
*.TIF
*.TIFF
*.GIF
*.DNG
*.MP4
*.MOV
*.M4V
*.AVI
*.MKV
*.WEBM
*.3GP
*.MTS

# Currently inert: tests/fixtures/isobmff.ts and jpeg.ts build hand-crafted
# byte-level parser inputs PROGRAMMATICALLY, in .ts, so nothing above ever
# matches anything under this path today — `git check-ignore -v` confirms
# no file here is ignored, negation or not. Kept as a forward-looking guard
# in case a fixture ever ships as an actual media-extension file (a real
# .jpg or .mp4, capped small) rather than code that builds one; the
# rationale for the fixtures themselves lives in their own header comments,
# there is no separate README here.
!/tests/fixtures/**

# Build + tooling
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
